# Coach speech (Traditional Chinese, Taiwan / Hong Kong): the appraisal after the game
# (src/coach/appraisal.cpp). Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang.
# Subtitle text only (the voice speaks the English line), so no ".spoken" overrides here.
# The appraisal is always positive and never blames.
#
# Placeholders: {moves} = full moves the game lasted ("{moves}回合"); {move} = one of the player's
# moves (figurine, "♘f3"); {n} its move number, said "第{n}回合" as in the opening texts
# ("我們在第{n}回合離開了已知的開局理論"); {crit_no} the same for the critical moment. Counted
# nouns come from common.lang ("{n:piece}" = "3個子", "{m:time}" = "5次", "{n:move}" = "3步",
# "{n:mistake}" = "3步錯著"). {acc} {acc_coach} {acc_phase} are written with a percent sign
# ("{acc}%"). {my} = a piece of the coach's, with its possessive ("我的馬"). {opening} = the
# opening's name from the opening texts ("義大利開局").
# Inserted names (see each use): {text} = appraisal.phase.* (a bare noun: 開局, 中局, 殘局) or
# appraisal.reason.* (a short cause after "和棋：" or before "，和棋"); {theme} = theme.* (an
# instruction without a final full stop, always after a colon: "值得練習：{theme}。"); {level} =
# appraisal.level.* (the level names of the interface, coach.level.*.name), put in 「」 by the
# sentence; {my:bare} = the coach's piece without 我的, where the sentence already says 我 ("我讓象…").

